    "description": "## Source of truth\n\nhttps://jumpr.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/JK/pages/269090817/03+User+Stories+Jira+Disposition\n\n## Outcome\n\nCentralize Deal lifecycle dates/history so action flows only change Status and shared automation owns tracking.\n\n## Fields\n\nUse Date fields:\n\n* Previous Deal Status;\n* Draft Date;\n* First Activated Date;\n* Active Date;\n* Paused Date;\n* Inactive Date;\n* Closed Date;\n* Archived Date;\n* Effective End Date.\n\nReview Required Date and Retired Date are no longer part of the target lifecycle.\n\n## Rules\n\n* On normal Deal creation in Draft, stamp Draft Date if blank.\n* Preserve an authorized historical Draft Date supplied for migration/remediation.\n* Previous Status + destination Date update only when Status actually changes.\n* First Activated Date is write-once.\n* Active Date updates on each actual transition to Active.\n* Entering Closed stamps Closed Date + Effective End Date.\n* Entering Archived stamps Archived Date + Effective End Date through shared end-state logic.\n* **Any transition to Active clears Effective End Date.**\n* Unrelated edits do not restamp lifecycle Dates.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. New Draft gets Draft Date once.\n2. Active → Paused stamps Paused Date.\n3. Paused → Active updates Active Date, preserves First Activated Date and clears Effective End Date.\n4. Active → Closed stamps Closed Date + Effective End Date.\n5. Closed → Active clears Effective End Date.\n6. Eligible state → Archived stamps Archived Date + Effective End Date.\n7. API/data-load transitions receive the same centralized lifecycle treatment.\n\n",
